#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188005 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188298 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1220ac85-068f-5685-ad04-7914a59641ba" :knowledge-point/title "Recovering the Joint PDF from a Joint CDF"}] :question/id #uuid "4af79cd3-8c50-533f-a744-3784a71a15dc" :question/math-academy-id "e-10117" :question/problem "The joint CDF of two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n${0,\\begin{vmatrix}x < 0ory < 0 \\\\ x^{2}(1 - e^{-y}),\\end{vmatrix}0 \\le x \\le 1, y \\ge 0; F_{Y}(y), \\mid x > 1, y \\ge 0$.\n\nFind the joint PDF $f(x,y)$ for $0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\; y \\geq 0$." :question/worked-solution "Since the partial derivatives of $F(x,y)$ are defined, the joint probability density function $f(x, y)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y) = \\dfrac{\\partial^2}{\\partial x \\partial y} F(x,y)\n$$\n\nFor\n\n$$\n0 \\leq x \\leq 1\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ny \\geq 0\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x, y) &= \\frac{∂^{2}}{∂x∂y}F(x, y) \\\\\n&= \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x^{2}(1 - e^{-y}))) \\\\\n&= \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(1 - e^{-y})) \\\\\n&= \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2}e^{-y}) \\\\\n&= e^{-y} \\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2}) \\\\\n&= e^{-y} \\cdot 2x \\\\\n&= 2xe^{-y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOtherwise,\n\n$$\nf(x,y) = 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{2xe^{-y},\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le x \\le 1, y \\ge 0 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188066 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188358 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aae311f3-6d07-5104-aa55-5d76b986510a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal CDF Using a Joint CDF"}] :question/id #uuid "731d3a2d-4853-52e4-9c86-3654dc66adab" :question/math-academy-id "e-10436" :question/problem "The joint CDF of two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$, for $(x,y) \\in [0,1] \\times [0,2]$, is given by\n\n$F(x,y)= \\dfrac{xy}{8}(2x^2+y)$.\n\nFind $F_X(x)$, the marginal CDF of $X$, for $0 \\leq x \\leq 1$." :question/worked-solution "The marginal CDF of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF_X(x) = F(x,\\infty) = \\lim\\limits_{y \\to \\infty} F(x,y)\n$$\n\nTherefore, for\n\n$$\n0\\leq x\\leq 1\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF_{X}(x) &= F(x, ∞) \\\\\n&= F(x, 2) \\\\\n&= (x(2))/(8)(2x^{2} + (2)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{4x}{8}(x^{2} + 1) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(x^{3} + x)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188212 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188277 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f96f4b28-61d0-5c7e-b779-104245fe26d4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Part of a Joint CDF from Marginal CDFs for Continuous Random Variables"}] :question/id #uuid "b48c754c-18c0-575f-bc6a-54f6fbdcec62" :question/math-academy-id "e-9223" :question/problem "The marginal CDFs of two continuous independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below.\n\n${1 - \\frac{1}{x},\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n\nFind the expression for the joint CDF when $x \\geq 1$ and $y\\geq 1$." :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are independent continuous random variables with marginal CDFs $F_X(x)$ and $F_Y(y)$, respectively, then the corresponding joint CDF of $F(x,y)$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y) = F_X(x) \\cdot F_Y (y)\n$$\n\nTherefore, for\n\n$$\nx \\geq 1\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ny \\geq 1\n$$\n\nthe joint CDF for our random variables is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(x, y) &= F_{X}(x) \\cdot F_{Y}(y) \\\\\n&= (1 - \\frac{1}{x})(1 - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y^{3}}}) \\\\\n&= 1 - \\frac{1}{x} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y^{3}}} + \\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{y^{3}}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the joint CDF is\n\n$$\n{1 - \\frac{1}{x} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y^{3}}} + \\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{y^{3}}},\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 1, y \\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188845 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188277 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f96f4b28-61d0-5c7e-b779-104245fe26d4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Part of a Joint CDF from Marginal CDFs for Continuous Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88e072e4-1274-5dc6-8872-75e1fe691d63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - \\frac{1}{x^{2}} - \\frac{1}{y} + \\frac{1}{x^{2}y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187351} {:answer/id #uuid "8ea5a171-ad63-55af-b709-dab096ef107f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + \\frac{1}{x^{2}y^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187352} {:answer/id #uuid "8fe864a7-574d-58e0-a408-6e5b48b4c235" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - \\frac{1}{x^{2}y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187353} {:answer/id #uuid "975df375-b55a-54f7-895c-b8ee4c9336c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - \\frac{2}{x^{2}} - \\frac{2}{y} + \\frac{1}{x^{2}y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187354} {:answer/id #uuid "e49c8732-9ee6-5112-9ca4-b18aedb2b9d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - \\frac{1}{x^{2}} - \\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187355}] :answer-field/id #uuid "b432ba9e-dcac-5433-8ff8-190ee8bb1ea7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187350}] :question/id #uuid "18e3d97c-1951-59bd-b3e7-0c892c88f04a" :question/math-academy-id "q-159316" :question/problem "The marginal CDFs of two continuous independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below.\n\n$F_{X}(x) = {1 - \\frac{1}{x^{2}},\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwiseF_{Y}(y) = {1 - \\frac{1}{y},\\begin{vmatrix}y \\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n\nFind the expression for the joint CDF when $x \\ge 1$ and $y \\ge 1$."}]}
